---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import { getEntry } from 'astro:content';

const siteEntry = await getEntry('site', 'site');
const siteData = siteEntry.data;

const PRIVACY_EMAIL = 'privacy@thirdwave.fun';
const MAILTO_URL = `mailto:${PRIVACY_EMAIL}`;
const LAST_UPDATED = 'November 18, 2026';
---

<Layout
	title="Third Wave — Privacy Policy"
	description="How Third Wave collects, processes, and uses your information when you visit thirdwave.fun or use our services."
	socialDescription="Third Wave Privacy Policy."
>
	<Header
		status={siteData.topBar.status}
		meta={siteData.topBar.meta}
		ticker={siteData.ticker}
		ctaHref={MAILTO_URL}
		ctaText="CONTACT US"
	/>

	<main>
		<article class="privacy">
			<p class="eyebrow">Legal</p>
			<h1 class="privacy-title">Privacy Policy</h1>
			<p class="updated">Last updated: {LAST_UPDATED}</p>

			<section>
				<h2>Introduction</h2>
				<p>
					Your Free Call Will End Soon, Co. (&ldquo;Company&rdquo;,
					&ldquo;we&rdquo;, &ldquo;us&rdquo;, &ldquo;our&rdquo;) is a Delaware
					corporation that offers its services under the brand name Third Wave.
					We have adopted this Privacy Policy to make it easy for
					you to understand what sorts of information we collect and how we use
					that information. This Privacy Policy discloses information we collect,
					process, and use when you visit our website at thirdwave.fun (the
					&ldquo;Site&rdquo;), use the Third Wave mobile application (the
					&ldquo;App&rdquo;), or use the software, products, and services we offer
					via the Site or the App (collectively, the &ldquo;Services&rdquo;). Please read
					this Privacy Policy carefully. If you do not consent to the practices
					detailed in this Privacy Policy you should not use the Services.
				</p>
				<p>
					We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time. All changes are
					effective immediately when we post them and we will use reasonable
					efforts to alert you about any changes by updating the &ldquo;Last
					updated&rdquo; date of this Privacy Policy. By continuing to use the
					Site, the App, or the Services after the date such revised Privacy Policy is posted,
					you will be subject to, and be deemed to have accepted, the changes
					therein.
				</p>
			</section>

			<section>
				<h2>Information we collect and how we collect it</h2>
				<p>
					While using our Services, we collect certain information that can be used to
					contact or identify you (&ldquo;Personal Information&rdquo;). The
					Personal Information we collect includes:
				</p>
				<dl>
					<dt>Name &amp; Contact Details</dt>
					<dd>
						Such as your email address (optional in the App) and display name, and
						any contact details you include in a support request. We do not ask for
						your date of birth.
					</dd>

					<dt>Account Information</dt>
					<dd>
						Such as your display name, your avatar (which can be a photo), the
						device ID the App uses to identify your Account, the email address you
						add to your Account if you choose to, and transaction information.
					</dd>

					<dt>Commercial Information</dt>
					<dd>
						When you buy a ticket, our payment processor Stripe collects your
						payment card details; we do not receive or store your full card number.
						We keep a record of each purchase (what you bought, when, where, and the
						amount).
					</dd>

					<dt>Device Information</dt>
					<dd>
						Such as your device&rsquo;s make, model, operating system, and screen
						size, and your IP address. On Android, the App asks for permission to
						use your device&rsquo;s precise location, which it needs to join a
						venue&rsquo;s Wi-Fi network. We do not store this location.
					</dd>

					<dt>Information Uploaded Through Use of Services</dt>
					<dd>
						Avatar photos, photos you take with in-game cameras, text you type into
						games, and live camera and microphone streams that some games send to
						the venue screen. We do not store live streams, other than as they
						appear in match clips.
					</dd>
					<dd>
						Reviews, reports about other players, and support tickets you send us,
						and gameplay data such as your scores, teams, results, and game stats.
						Our Services do not have chat. Please note that your display name,
						avatar, and scores can be seen by other players and the public, and
						avatar photos are stored at public links.
					</dd>
				</dl>

				<p>We collect this information in the following ways:</p>
				<ul>
					<li>
						You may voluntarily provide us certain information when you interact
						with the Site or use our Services.
					</li>
					<li>
						Our servers automatically collect certain information from your browser
						or device when you use our online Services (&ldquo;Log Data&rdquo;).
						Log Data includes information such as your device&rsquo;s IP address,
						browser type, browser version, language, connection type, and the time
						and date of your request.
					</li>
					<li>
						Our service providers that administer Services for us, for example our
						hosting provider(s) and analytics and advertising measurement
						providers, may provide us access to certain information we request from
						time to time.
					</li>
					<li>
						Users of our software may disclose to us certain information that they
						collect from you with your consent.
					</li>
					<li>
						We and our service providers use cookies, pixels, and other
						technologies to track your Internet activity on our Site. We do not use
						them in the App.
					</li>
				</ul>
				<h3>High-score boards</h3>
				<p>
					When you play a Third Wave game that keeps high scores, we record each
					match: the venue, the cabinet, the time, the course, the team names and
					the team scores and stats. We keep these match results with no time limit.
					Team names, as a team&rsquo;s captain chose them or a house name when none
					was chosen, are kept with the match whether or not anyone said yes. Apart
					from a team name (below), your username is kept on the high-score boards
					only if you say yes. When you set a record, your phone may ask you after
					the match. A yes belongs to the username: we then keep that username with
					its team, whether the team won, awards, game stats and best results, for
					that match and for later games played under that username at any Third
					Wave venue, until it is taken off. We keep the yes itself, with its time,
					until then. If you say no, or do not answer, the boards keep nothing of
					yours from that match. Your per-match details, and your daily totals with
					the time of your last game that day, are deleted after 35 and 30 days.
					After that we keep all-time totals and best results for each venue and for
					all venues together, with the day each best was set and the day of the
					latest game. Usernames and scores may be shown on screens at the venue
					where they were played and at other Third Wave venues. After you say yes,
					the end of a game of Gary&rsquo;s Party Line offers TAKE ME OFF THE
					BOARDS. It takes your username and everything kept for it off every board
					within a day, and you may be asked again at your next record. NEVER
					INCLUDE ME does the same, and you are never asked again; we keep a coded
					form of your username, and the day you chose this, so we can keep it off.
					We can undo this if you ask, but what was taken off does not come back. A
					team name a captain gave that is your username (capitals and spaces aside)
					is blanked on past matches when your username is taken off, and on later
					matches too after NEVER INCLUDE ME. Game pictures and videos, which are
					made for every player, are deleted after about 14 days, and backups are
					cleared of your username within 30 days. To take any username off,
					including one you used before or one that never said yes, ask us at the
					address below.
				</p>
				<p>
					<strong>Global leaderboard.</strong> The App also has a global
					leaderboard that shows every player&rsquo;s display name and points,
					whether or not you said yes to the high-score boards above. To ask us to
					remove your display name from it, e-mail
					<a href={MAILTO_URL}>{PRIVACY_EMAIL}</a>.
				</p>
				<p>
					<strong>In-game photos.</strong> Photos you take with in-game cameras are
					stored on the venue&rsquo;s computer at hard-to-guess links that anyone
					with the link can open without logging in. We keep them until the show is
					retired, 90 days by default.
				</p>
			</section>

			<section>
				<h2>How we use information we collect</h2>
				<p>
					We use your Personal Information for the following purposes, and as
					otherwise described in this Privacy Policy or at the time of collection:
				</p>
				<dl>
					<dt>Delivery of Services</dt>
					<dd>
						We may use your Personal Information in order to achieve our legitimate
						business interest of delivering Services you request or to fulfill
						contractual obligations to you. We may correlate data from separate
						sources (e.g., our Site and our App) for purposes of delivering the
						Services.
					</dd>

					<dt>Promotion</dt>
					<dd>
						We may use your Personal Information to create and effectively promote
						our Services to you and others. If you request to receive marketing
						communications, you may unsubscribe from those communications using the
						&ldquo;unsubscribe&rdquo; link in the applicable communication.
					</dd>

					<dt>Site Optimization</dt>
					<dd>
						We use analytics and search engine providers to assist us in the
						improvement and optimization of our Site and provide information to
						providers such as Google and Cloudflare for these purposes.
					</dd>

					<dt>To comply with laws and regulations</dt>
					<dd>
						We may use your Personal Information as we believe necessary or
						appropriate to comply with applicable laws, lawful requests, and legal
						process, such as to respond to subpoenas or requests from government
						authorities.
					</dd>

					<dt>For compliance, fraud prevention and safety</dt>
					<dd>
						We may use your Personal Information and disclose it to law enforcement,
						government authorities, and private parties as we believe necessary or
						appropriate to: (a) protect our, your or others&rsquo; rights, privacy,
						safety or property (including by making and defending legal claims); (b)
						audit our internal processes for compliance with legal and contractual
						requirements; and (c) protect, investigate and deter against
						fraudulent, harmful, unauthorized, unethical or illegal activity,
						including cyber-attacks and identity theft.
					</dd>

					<dt>For any other purpose you consent to at the time of collection</dt>
					<dd>
						Provided that if we intend to subsequently use your Personal
						Information for a different purpose, we will obtain your consent for
						such different purpose.
					</dd>
				</dl>
			</section>

			<section>
				<h2>How and when we share information</h2>
				<p>
					We may share your Personal Information, for the purposes outlined above,
					with the following categories of recipients:
				</p>
				<dl>
					<dt>Service providers</dt>
					<dd>
						We share your Personal Information with service providers to enable
						such parties to perform functions on our behalf and under our
						instructions in order to carry out the purposes identified above.
						Specifically, we disclose your Personal Information with the following
						categories of service providers:
						<ul>
							<li>Hosting providers, including database and function hosting, as well as web servers;</li>
							<li>Network-security providers;</li>
							<li>Authentication providers;</li>
							<li>Email facilitation; and</li>
							<li>Payment processors.</li>
						</ul>
					</dd>

					<dt>Affiliated Companies</dt>
					<dd>
						We may also share your Personal Information with our subsidiaries,
						affiliates and other related companies for purposes consistent with
						this Privacy Policy and providing you with our Services.
					</dd>

					<dt>Business reorganization</dt>
					<dd>
						We may share your Personal Information with any corporate purchaser or
						prospect to the extent permitted by law as part of any merger,
						acquisition, sale of company assets, or transition of service to another
						provider, as well as in the event of insolvency, bankruptcy, or
						receivership in which Personal Information would be transferred as an
						asset of Company.
					</dd>

					<dt>Mandatory Disclosures and Legal Rights</dt>
					<dd>
						We may share your Personal Information to comply with applicable laws
						and regulations, to respond to a subpoena, search warrant or other
						legal or governmental request for information. We also share Personal
						Information to establish or protect our legal rights, property, or
						safety, or the rights, property, or safety of others, or to defend
						against legal claims.
					</dd>
				</dl>
				<p>
					We have not sold Personal Information for money in the past 12 months,
					and we do not intend to. We do let Meta collect information through the
					Meta Pixel on our Site (see &ldquo;Cookies and similar technologies&rdquo;
					below) so we can measure and advertise our Services. Under California and
					some other US state laws, that may count as &ldquo;selling&rdquo; or
					&ldquo;sharing&rdquo; Personal Information for targeted advertising. In
					the past 12 months the categories involved were identifiers (such as
					cookie IDs and IP address) and internet activity (such as pages viewed and
					clicks to sign up or contact us), disclosed to Meta Platforms, Inc. You can
					opt out at any time; see &ldquo;Your privacy choices&rdquo; below. Google
					Analytics processes data for us as our service provider under
					Google&rsquo;s data processing terms, and we have turned off Google&rsquo;s
					use of that data for its own purposes.
				</p>
				<p>
					We may also disclose your Personal Information for the following purposes,
					which are not a sale: (i) if you direct us to share your Personal
					Information, (ii) disclosures as part of a merger or asset sale, and (iii)
					as otherwise required or permitted by applicable law. We do not offer
					financial incentives associated with our collection, use, or disclosure of
					your Personal Information.
				</p>
			</section>

			<section>
				<h2>Cookies and similar technologies</h2>
				<p>
					Cookies are small files a website stores in your browser. Our Site uses
					these:
				</p>
				<dl>
					<dt>Google Analytics (Google LLC) &mdash; <code>_ga</code>, <code>_ga_*</code></dt>
					<dd>
						Measures how visitors use the Site: pages viewed, time on page, the
						device and browser used, and approximate location from your IP address.
						Kept for up to 2 years. Google processes this data as our service
						provider.
					</dd>

					<dt>Meta Pixel (Meta Platforms, Inc.) &mdash; <code>_fbp</code>, <code>_fbc</code></dt>
					<dd>
						Measures visits and actions such as signing up for our list or clicking
						to contact us, so we can measure and target advertising on Meta&rsquo;s
						platforms. Meta may also use this information for its own purposes under
						its own privacy policy. Kept for up to 90 days.
					</dd>

					<dt>Your privacy choice &mdash; <code>tw-consent</code></dt>
					<dd>
						Remembers whether you allowed or declined the cookies above, so we do
						not ask again. Stored in your browser until you clear it.
					</dd>

					<dt>Our host (Cloudflare, Inc.)</dt>
					<dd>
						May set cookies that are strictly necessary to protect the Site from
						abuse. These cannot be turned off.
					</dd>
				</dl>
				<p>
					If you visit from the European Economic Area, the United Kingdom or
					Switzerland, the Google Analytics and Meta Pixel cookies are not set unless
					you accept them. Everywhere else they are set when you visit, and you can
					turn them off at any time; see &ldquo;Your privacy choices&rdquo; below.
					You can also block or delete cookies in your browser&rsquo;s settings.
				</p>
			</section>

			<section id="your-privacy-choices">
				<h2>Your privacy choices</h2>
				<p>
					Use the <a href="/privacy#your-privacy-choices" data-tw-choices>Your
					Privacy Choices</a> link at the bottom of any page on our Site to turn
					analytics and advertising cookies on or off. Turning them off opts you out
					of the sale or sharing of your Personal Information for targeted
					advertising, and, if you are in the European Economic Area, the United
					Kingdom or Switzerland, withdraws your consent. We then stop loading
					Google Analytics and the Meta Pixel and delete their cookies. Your choice
					applies to the browser and device you make it on.
				</p>
				<p>
					We honor the Global Privacy Control (GPC) signal. If your browser sends
					it, we treat it as a request to opt out of sale and sharing, and we do not
					load Google Analytics or the Meta Pixel.
				</p>
				<p>
					You can also ask us to opt you out by e-mailing
					<a href={MAILTO_URL}>{PRIVACY_EMAIL}</a>.
				</p>
			</section>

			<section>
				<h2>Your rights</h2>
				<p>
					Depending on your jurisdiction, you may have the following rights,
					subject to some exceptions:
				</p>
				<dl>
					<dt>Right to know and access</dt>
					<dd>
						To know what Personal Information we have collected about you, where it
						came from, why we collected it, who we disclosed it to, and to get a
						copy of it.
					</dd>

					<dt>Right to delete</dt>
					<dd>To ask us to delete Personal Information we collected from you.</dd>

					<dt>Right to correct</dt>
					<dd>To ask us to correct inaccurate Personal Information about you.</dd>

					<dt>Right to opt out of sale and sharing</dt>
					<dd>
						To opt out of the sale of your Personal Information and its sharing or
						processing for targeted advertising; see &ldquo;Your privacy
						choices&rdquo; above.
					</dd>

					<dt>Right to limit use of sensitive Personal Information</dt>
					<dd>
						We use the precise location from the Android App only to let you join a
						venue&rsquo;s Wi-Fi network, and we do not use or disclose sensitive
						Personal Information for any purpose that would give rise to this right.
					</dd>

					<dt>Right to non-discrimination</dt>
					<dd>
						We will not deny you Services, charge you a different price, or give you
						a different quality of Services because you used any of these rights.
					</dd>
				</dl>
				<p>
					<strong>How to make a request.</strong> E-mail us at
					<a href={MAILTO_URL}>{PRIVACY_EMAIL}</a>, or use our
					<a href="/delete-account">account deletion page</a> to delete your
					account. We will confirm we received your request within 10 business days
					and respond within 45 days; if we need more time (up to another 45 days)
					we will tell you why. We will ask for information to verify your identity,
					such as confirming the e-mail address you used with us. You may use an
					authorized agent to make a request for you; we may ask the agent for proof
					that you authorized them, and ask you to verify your identity directly.
				</p>
				<p>
					<strong>Appeals.</strong> If we decline your request, you may appeal by
					replying to our decision or e-mailing <a href={MAILTO_URL}>{PRIVACY_EMAIL}</a>
					with &ldquo;Appeal&rdquo; in the subject line. We will answer within the
					time your state&rsquo;s law requires. If you disagree with the outcome,
					you may contact your state&rsquo;s Attorney General.
				</p>
				<p>
					<strong>California &ldquo;Shine the Light&rdquo;.</strong> California
					residents may ask us once a year, free of charge, for information about
					Personal Information we disclosed to third parties for their direct
					marketing purposes in the prior calendar year. E-mail
					<a href={MAILTO_URL}>{PRIVACY_EMAIL}</a>.
				</p>
			</section>

			<section>
				<h2>Protection of your information</h2>
				<p>
					We take our responsibility to protect your information very seriously.
					While no data transmission is guaranteed to be 100% secure, we use
					reasonable and appropriate security measures and practices to protect
					your Personal Information from unauthorized access, use, alteration, and
					destruction.
				</p>
			</section>

			<section>
				<h2>Data retention</h2>
				<p>
					We retain Personal Information for as long as necessary for the relevant
					purpose for which that Personal Information was provided or collected,
					unless a longer retention period is required or permitted by law (such as
					tax, accounting, or other legal requirements). This will be for as long
					as we provide access to the Services to you.
				</p>
				<p>
					After you have closed your account or ceased using the Services, we
					delete your Personal Information, except that we keep your play history,
					tickets, reviews, and support tickets in anonymized form that is no longer
					linked to you. We may also retain Personal Information
					where reasonably necessary to comply with our legal obligations
					(including law enforcement requests), meet regulatory requirements,
					maintain security, prevent fraud and abuse, resolve disputes, enforce our
					contracts, or fulfill your request to &ldquo;unsubscribe&rdquo; from
					further messages from us.
				</p>
				<p>
					You can request deletion of your account and associated data at any time
					via our <a href="/delete-account">account deletion page</a>.
				</p>
				<p>
					Deleting your account does not delete photos you took with in-game
					cameras at a venue; those are kept until the show is retired (90 days by
					default), as described above. To ask us to delete one sooner, e-mail
					<a href={MAILTO_URL}>{PRIVACY_EMAIL}</a>.
				</p>
				<p>
					Per-match high-score details are deleted after 35 days and daily totals
					after 30 days; all-time totals and best results are kept with no time
					limit, with only the day of each best and of the latest game. Usernames
					are kept on the high-score boards only after a yes, until taken off; see
					&ldquo;High-score boards&rdquo; above.
				</p>
			</section>

			<section>
				<h2>Other sites, mobile applications and services</h2>
				<p>
					The Services may contain links to other websites and online services
					operated by third parties. These links are not an endorsement of, or
					representation that we are affiliated with, any third party. In addition,
					our content may be included on web pages or online services that are not
					associated with us. We do not control third party websites or online
					services, and we are not responsible for their actions. Other websites
					and services follow different rules regarding the collection, use and
					sharing of your Personal Information. We encourage you to read the privacy
					policies of the other websites and online services you use.
				</p>
			</section>

			<section>
				<h2>Data collected from minors</h2>
				<p>
					Our Services are not for children under 13, and we do not knowingly
					collect Personal Information from them. Players aged 13 to 17 may use the
					Services only with a parent or legal guardian&rsquo;s permission, as our
					<a href="/terms">Terms of Service</a> describe. If we learn that we have
					collected Personal Information from a child under 13, we will deactivate
					the account and take reasonable measures to promptly delete that data. If
					you believe we have, please contact us at
					<a href={MAILTO_URL}>{PRIVACY_EMAIL}</a>.
				</p>
			</section>

			<section>
				<h2>Contact us</h2>
				<p>
					For more information about our privacy practices, if you have questions,
					or if you would like to make a complaint, please contact us by e-mail at
					<a href={MAILTO_URL}>{PRIVACY_EMAIL}</a>.
				</p>
			</section>
		</article>
	</main>

	<Footer
		production={siteData.footer.production}
		copyrightHolder={siteData.footer.copyrightHolder}
		youtube={siteData.social.youtube}
		instagram={siteData.social.instagram}
	/>
</Layout>

<style>
	main {
		flex: 1;
		display: flex;
		flex-direction: column;
	}

	.privacy {
		padding: 64px 40px 80px;
		max-width: 740px;
		margin: 0 auto;
		width: 100%;
	}

	.eyebrow {
		font-family: var(--font-label);
		font-size: 11px;
		font-weight: 500;
		letter-spacing: 0.18em;
		text-transform: uppercase;
		color: #888;
		margin-bottom: 24px;
	}

	.privacy-title {
		font-family: var(--font-display);
		font-weight: 800;
		font-size: clamp(36px, 6vw, 56px);
		line-height: 0.98;
		letter-spacing: -0.025em;
		text-transform: uppercase;
		color: var(--color-text);
		margin-bottom: 16px;
	}

	.updated {
		font-family: var(--font-label);
		font-size: 11px;
		letter-spacing: 0.14em;
		text-transform: uppercase;
		color: #888;
		margin-bottom: 56px;
	}

	section {
		margin-bottom: 48px;
	}

	section h2 {
		font-family: var(--font-display);
		font-weight: 600;
		font-size: 22px;
		letter-spacing: -0.01em;
		color: var(--color-text);
		margin-bottom: 16px;
	}

	section h3 {
		font-family: var(--font-display);
		font-weight: 600;
		font-size: 17px;
		color: var(--color-text);
		margin: 28px 0 12px;
	}

	section p {
		font-family: var(--font-sans);
		font-size: 15px;
		line-height: 1.65;
		color: #b3b3b3;
		margin-bottom: 16px;
	}

	section p:last-child {
		margin-bottom: 0;
	}

	dl {
		margin: 0 0 8px;
	}

	dt {
		font-family: var(--font-sans);
		font-weight: 600;
		font-size: 15px;
		color: var(--color-text);
		margin-bottom: 4px;
	}

	dd {
